  "configuration_id": "config_021",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_020 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) is the current best at 0.542 acc, outperforming both the resnet50 variant (config_010, 0.525) and the transformer-aggregation variant (config_019, 0.520). This establishes scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool as the strongest backbone. The only untested dimension within this best-performing setup is the fusion method (all three completed experiments used weighted fusion). Question: Does concat fusion outperform or match weighted fusion when paired with the best backbone? This is a minimal, focused change (only fusion: weighted→concat) that directly tests whether we can push accuracy above 0.542 or confirm weighted as optimal. Rationale: With 6 experiments left, exploiting the clearly best configuration by testing its last unexplored hyperparameter is the highest-information-per-cost move. Expected cost is similar to config_020 (~2.9–3.0 GPU hours) since the architecture is identical and concat fusion is marginally cheaper than weighted fusion. If concat matches or beats weighted, we lock in the best multimodal multiprofile setup; if not, we confirm weighted and can pivot to exploring alternative RNA encoders (pca_n2000, scvi_n200) in subsequent experiments."
}

